{"author":{"id":"b409816c5cd5ab140d1d52eb33aace35de44952bb794b19806fd57f6ecb1ace9"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1791534551,"nonce":"RsJTIghJU3+pMu1la/W8qVMApjQ=","title":"HIR: version virtual-object loops with exits to the generic path","message":"After combining guarded reads (cdd2ecfa1c1f4fc65a5a6fc52ecd1f378dd8852a3e48a01fe12681b436709477), op_overload still carries virtual/backing state and mutable metamethod guards through its hot loop. The audited main retains 100 HIR blocks, 108 phis and 44 conditional branches. Whole-function Cranelift frame reservation remains 624 bytes; cold materialization and generic arithmetic paths are retained.\n\nThe existing loop_specialize pass rejects bodies above 128 instructions/phis and rejects direct calls or allocations before it tries a constant-state candidate. It also requires every reachable backedge to retain the selected constant. This excludes virtual-object loops whose ordinary typed backedge remains virtual but whose generic arithmetic path produces an opaque object.\n\nInvestigate a bounded specialized loop entered with a runtime virtual-state guard. Keep typed reads in scalar SSA values. Backedges that change the virtual state must return to the original header with correctly merged state, including backing pointers and every field; do not assume the state is invariant across effectful fallback paths. Preserve materialization, mutable metatable checks, nullable inputs, retained aliases and OSR. Only move operand/metadata loads when alias and effect analysis proves they stay valid on the specialized path. Assess independent numeric lanes for Cranelift SIMD after the fast loop is straight enough.\n\nValidate interpreter-first tiering, both native backends, zero-trip loops, repeated opaque-to-virtual transitions, native OSR and all supported kernel outputs. Compare frozen binaries in short and long runs with LLVM disabled on ARM64 and the NUC; no Cargo builds during or between samples. The current guarded-read work does not establish a short-run win or a broad Python improvement.","files":null}]}